            <div xml:id="d113">

                <pb facs="0289" n="155" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg155"/>

                <head>No. 113.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hosmer to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States in Central America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-06-09"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi>
                            9, 1888</date>. (Received June 28.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 818.].</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your instructions numbered 574, of April 30, 1888, furnishing many good and
                    sufficient reasons why the clause in the annulled treaty between the United
                    States and Guatemala, relating to peace and friendship, should be still <pb
                        facs="0290" n="156" xml:id="pg156"/> in force, and I beg respectfully to
                    inclose to you a copy of my note addressed to the minister for foreign affairs
                    of Guatemala, dated June 6, 1888, in which I attempt to impart your views to
                    that Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James R. Hosmer</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d113-a1.xml" xpointer="d113-a1"/>
            </div>
